hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2679","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashjaj and Salm ibn Junadah. Salm said: \Narrated to us Ibn Idris"," and al-Ashjaj said: 'Narrated to me Abdullah ibn Idris"," and he wrote this hadith for me and sent it to me.' He [Ibn Idris] said: 'Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ishaq"," from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr"," from his father"," from Asma bint Abi Bakr (RA).'\nShe said: \""We set out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as Hajj pilgrims"," and the pack camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the pack camel of Abu Bakr (RA) were shared between them. We stopped at al-Araj"," and our pack camel was with Abu Bakr's servant. She said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat down"," and Aisha sat beside him"," and Abu Bakr sat beside the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the other side"," and I sat beside my father waiting for his servant and our pack camel to come to us. Then the servant came walking"," and his camel was not with him. He said: \""So Abu Bakr said to him: 'Where is your camel?' He replied: 'It was lost from me last night.' So Abu Bakr stood up to him"," beating him"," and saying: 'You lost a single camel"," and you are a man capable of guarding it!' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did nothing but smile and say: 'Look at this person in the state of ihram"," and what he is doing.'\nThis is the hadith reported by al-Ashjaj. Salm said: \""Our pack camel and the pack camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were the same.\"" Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Yusuf ibn Musa"," who said: \""Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Idris"," who informed us of Muhammad ibn Ishaq"," with a similar narration.\"" Al-Dawraqi said: \""The pack camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the pack camel of Abu Bakr (RA) were the same","\"" and Yusuf said: \""The pack camel of Abu Bakr (RA) and the pack camel of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were the same.\"""""
